{"request_sha256": "6ac2ce28ce1a78e207be136182e394f5615823d3af8cb7a554cdd5dfeaa85d90", "prompt_sha256": "41ce0317d48d66c48f27d90ac1b32c243e3040b9e4e995bf9fe78793a495333b", "dispatched_prompt_sha256": "f7f68d933064560875affac11e65c1f2a3d52c387116221c17fe2640a69b0092", "schema_sha256": "16e85d59e1b5b494dcb4212f6a717d121774f1597ba7eb3b65eaf0b4c9e5ff18", "model": "opus", "model_identity_basis": "claude CLI result event modelUsage key: claude-opus-5-5", "effort": "medium", "status": "ok", "forbidden_tools": [], "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 13076}, "answer": {"passes": ["pass", "pass", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "pass", "pass", "pass", "pass", "pass", "unknown", "fail", "fail", "pass", "pass", "fail", "fail", "pass", "pass", "fail", "fail", "pass", "pass", "pass", "pass"], "defects": [{"defect": "On seeds 1 and 42, the fronds are straight, stiff rays. The crown reads as a spiky starburst or ball, not the rosette of long arching fronds seen in reference-0. The lowest fronds angle down only about 30-45° instead of hanging steeply. Frond length is small next to the very tall trunk.", "trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds"}, {"defect": "Frond shape fails the owner's first priority. The fronds are not arching, the lowest ones do not droop far enough, and they are short relative to the trunk.", "trait_id": null}, {"defect": "The trunk is a smooth shaft. The leaf bases appear as sparse, round-capped cylindrical pegs set in a single file along the trunk (render-0, render-1, render-2, render-3). There is no dense spiral diamond lattice of blunt wedge-shaped stubs with flat outer faces, as in reference-1 and reference-2.", "trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern"}, {"defect": "There is no fibrous matting between the leaf bases. The trunk surface is smooth and untextured in the P-BASE close view (render-3).", "trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting"}, {"defect": "The collar under the crown hangs against the upper trunk, but it is grey-green like the living foliage. It is not brown to grey, and there is no abrupt change from living to dead fronds, so it does not read as dead fronds.", "trait_id": "dead-frond-skirt"}], "observations": ["The finish of all renders is at or above the spruce anchor's catalogue floor. The anchor is used for finish only, not for morphology.", "render-3 (P-BASE) is marked visibility 'hidden' in the metadata, but the image clearly shows the trunk surface and pegs, so it was assessed as shown.", "In render-3 the trunk looks faceted, with a flat dark face and a hard edge, rather than round. It still reads as a round column at whole-tree distance.", "Frond colour depends on the view. The whole-tree views (render-0, render-1) read very dark green, close to black. The P-TRUNK view of the same seed-1 geometry (render-2) reads sage grey-green.", "The trunk is straight and vertical with near-constant diameter and a slight widening at the base. Reference-0 shows a lean and curve, but that is recorded as acceptable variation (trunk-lean-and-curve), and the owner asks for straight.", "The trunk is very tall compared with crown spread and frond length, more so than in reference-0 (crown-silhouette-proportions, a variation trait).", "Missing epiphytes is acceptable variation and matches the owner's bare-trunk requirement.", "fruit-clusters-pendent is a known gap (fn-111) and was not assessed."], "findings": [{"observation": "Both seeds show about 30-40 fronds radiating from one apex. The newest fronds stand upright and the lower ones angle down, but every frond is a straight ray with no arch. Reference-0 shows long recurved fronds with the lowest hanging almost vertically.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds"}, {"observation": "The owner's frond priority fails. The fronds do not arch, the lowest do not droop far enough, and frond length is short relative to trunk height.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Frond length and arching or droop curvature may be set too low.", "trait_id": null}, {"observation": "A rosette of pinnate fronds at the apex, with lower fronds below the crown base, is present on both seeds.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": null}, {"observation": "Leaflets are stiff and sharp-pointed, set at varied angles, and give the frond margin a bristly outline. They are somewhat broader and more widely spaced than the narrow linear leaflets in the references.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow"}, {"observation": "The leaf bases are sparse cylindrical pegs with round caps, set in a vertical file on a smooth trunk. There is no tessellated diamond lattice of wedge-shaped stubs.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern"}, {"observation": "The close view shows no fibre or husk between the leaf bases.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting"}, {"observation": "Both seeds have a single unbranched stem. The pegs are short stubs and do not read as branches.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem"}, {"observation": "The trunk is straight with near-constant diameter on both seeds.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": null}, {"observation": "Nothing grows on the trunk: no foliage, branches or epiphytes. The only additions are the leaf-base pegs, which are intended trunk organs.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": null}, {"observation": "Seed-1 fronds read grey-green in render-2. In the whole-tree views, seed 1 and seed 42 read very dark green, close to black, with only faint grey-green highlights. Seed 42 has no second view to settle this.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-1"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "The whole-tree lighting or backlighting may darken the foliage.", "trait_id": null}, {"observation": "The collar under the crown is present but grey-green, the same colour family as the living fronds. It is not brown.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "dead-frond-skirt"}, {"observation": "At whole-tree distance the trunk reads uniform grey-brown with a mauve cast, matching reference-0's distant read. Stub faces are not lighter than the surrounding trunk at close range.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-3", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "trunk-colour-and-weathering"}, {"observation": "Both seeds show a slight widening where the trunk meets the ground.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "basal-flare"}, {"observation": "No fruit is drawn. This is a known gap (fn-111) and was not assessed.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null, "trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent"}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "The fronds radiate from the apex but are straight and short, forming a starburst rather than long fronds that arch and droop."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The leaflets are stiff, pointed, set at varied angles and bristly at the margin. Their extra width is acceptable variation."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Sparse cylindrical pegs on a smooth trunk, with no diamond lattice of wedge-shaped stubs."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "No fibrous matting; the trunk surface is smooth."}, {"trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "A single unbranched stem of near-constant diameter."}, {"trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["reference-0"], "explanation": "Known gap (fn-111); not assessed."}, {"trait_id": "dead-frond-skirt", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "The collar is present but grey-green like the living fronds, with no brown colour and no change from living to dead."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-colour-and-weathering", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "At whole-tree distance the trunk reads uniform grey-brown with a mauve cast. Lighter weathered stub faces are an optional refinement."}, {"trait_id": "basal-flare", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "A slight widening at the base is visible on both seeds."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-lean-and-curve", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-1"], "explanation": "The trunk is straight and vertical, within the observed range and what the owner wants."}, {"trait_id": "frond-colour-range", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Grey-green in render-2, but very dark green in the whole-tree views; the lighting makes this ambiguous."}, {"trait_id": "epiphytes-on-trunk", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Not drawn. This is acceptable variation, since reference-0 also has none, and it matches the owner's bare-trunk requirement."}, {"trait_id": "crown-silhouette-proportions", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "The crown is wide next to the trunk width, but fronds are short next to the very tall trunk. Ratios cannot be measured reliably."}, {"trait_id": "crown-shaft-absent", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1"], "explanation": "No smooth crownshaft; the frond bases sit directly on the trunk under the collar."}]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system","subtype":"init","cwd":"/home/daniel/Projects/telperion/.worktrees/fn-80-the-gap-loops-first-live-run","session_id":"bb93c47e-2033-4615-b2cb-819dbf4b62f9","tools":["StructuredOutput"],"mcp_servers":[],"model":"claude-opus-5-5","permissionMode":"default","slash_commands":["deep-research","design","design-sync","dataviz","update-config","verify","debug","code-review","simplify","batch","fewer-permission-prompts","doctor","loop","schedule","claude-api","workflow-authoring","run","run-skill-generator","advisor","agents","auto-mode-setup","autocompact","clear","color","compact","config","output-style","context","effort","fast","heapdump"